\title{sizeSpectraFit: a streamlined R package for fitting size spectra to ecological data}
\description{
Provides code for fitting size spectra to ecological data using maximum likelihood methods. This is aimed to be a user-friendly version written from scratch with a focus on users applying methods to their data. The methods used are described and simulation tested in [1] Edwards et al. (Testing and recommending methods for fitting size spectra to data, Methods in Ecology and Evolution, 2017, 8:57-67) and [2] Edwards et al. (Accounting for the bin structure of data removes bias when fitting size spectra, Marine Ecology Progress Series, 2020, 636:19-33). See the GitHub site for more details, including rendered versions of the vignettes.
